  "raw": " DC Comics' The Official Magazine, Edge, GamePro , IGN, GiantBomb, IGN, Joker's Arcade, Kotaku , PC Gamer, 128 Knights, ScreenRant , for Windows PC, Symphonic gaming magazine Cross Gamerand DobreXpress.\n\nTwilight Princess marked a major turning point for Nintendo. It introduced motion controls alongside an entirely new world-set adventure. The RPG element weakened and the action game equivalent strengthened -aimed at challenging even experienced players like it did younger gamers otherwise uninterested in such content. All the charm of the past, but with a more mature story - unheard off until this point- more freedom of gameplay -seamlessly integrated into Link's combat system obvious value, tight controls, and nonlinear progression. Once again innovative. With no equally exciting successor due for several years, the series continued development measuredly nonetheless- focusing on quality rather than quantity. That gives me the idea that they may have left behind something but haven't left quite",
  "serialized": "DC Comics' The Official Magazine, Edge, GamePro , IGN, GiantBomb, IGN, Joker's Arcade, Kotaku , PC Gamer, 128 Knights, ScreenRant , for Windows PC, Symphonic gaming magazine Cross Gamerand DobreXpress. Twilight Princess marked a major turning point for Nintendo. It introduced motion controls alongside an entirely new world-set adventure. The RPG element weakened and the action game equivalent strengthened -aimed at challenging even experienced players like it did younger gamers otherwise uninterested in such content. All the charm of the past, but with a more mature story - unheard off until this point- more freedom of gameplay -seamlessly integrated into Link's combat system obvious value, tight controls, and nonlinear progression. Once again innovative. With no equally exciting successor due for several years, the series continued development measuredly nonetheless- focusing on quality rather than quantity. That gives me the idea that they may have left behind something but haven't left quite",
